# Check out text with LF line endings on every platform, so the files on disk are the text solc hashes
# into each contract's metadata. Foundry turns CRLF into LF before it compiles, so with it a CRLF checkout
# builds the same bytes; a tool that hands the files to solc as they are would not. A submodule follows
# its own attributes and the local git config, not this file.
* text=auto eol=lf
